  "brocante": {
   "name": "La brocante · The Flea Market",
   "room_id": "R_adj_time_01",
   "image": "brocante/brocante.jpg",
   "alt": "A Sunday flea market inside the village market hall, under a high glass roof on green iron arches, with striped stall awnings all around. A big two-story junk wagon stands in the middle and everyone is busy on it. On the roof two children lift down a little canoe carrying a mystery package, and a boy holds up one red pitcher beside a row of white pitchers. On the deck a pair of teddies share a seesaw, a boy shines up one boot (the dusty next ones dangle below), a king and a jester puppet act well in a little curtained theater and a fortune-teller sees a tiny rocket blast off in her crystal ball. Below, a toddler pushes a sweet pink-and-blue ice-cream van, a grandmother haggles over a cracked old rocking horse, a grandfather shows off his everyday coat and cap and a boy winds a brass gramophone. On the left a stone archway leads back out to the market square and a little shed has a red door; on the right a cottage has a green door and a blue door.",
