  "souvenirs": {
   "name": "Le stand des souvenirs · The Keepsake Stall",
   "room_id": "R_adj_time_02",
   "image": "brocante/souvenirs.jpg",
   "backTo": "brocante",
   "alt": "Inside a blue-and-white striped keepsake tent under the market hall's glass roof on a rainy day, seen from above, villagers crowd round a big round table. A granny pours tea from a plain brown teapot, a carpenter has just sawn a little stool where a ray of light falls, a girl opens a book of pressed flowers and an artist polishes a swirly modern silver sculpture. On the table a curving row of dominoes topples and a boy clicks a Newton's cradle. In front, a girl unpacks nesting dolls one after another, a man rolls a round stone wheel, a boy shakes a jar of shifting sand with an ant inside, a lone white swan sighs in a puddle and an odd striped sock falls into a laundry basket. The red door on the left leads back to the flea market; on the right a glass-fronted display cabinet stands on a side table.",
